# perl — static, -Uusedl (no dynamic loader on the disc, so no XS .so loading;
# any XS module would need to be baked into the binary via static_ext — see
# monolith-perl ebuild). Built with arsv/perl-cross driving vanilla perl
# (Gentoo's dev-lang/perl Configure is cross-hostile). No threads, no CPAN
# client. CGI.pm 4.10 (removed from perl core in 5.22) is baked in as a
# PURE-PERL rider for the guestbook's param()/header() — pinned specifically
# to 4.10 because every CGI.pm release from 4.11 onward hard-depends on
# HTML::Entities, which ships inside the XS HTML-Parser distribution; 4.10 is
# the newest release with zero XS in its dependency tree (verified against
# its Makefile.PL and a tarball-wide *.xs/*.c/*.h grep).
# DBI 1.651 + DBD::SQLite 1.78 are baked in via the same static_ext
# mechanism (SP5 P3, un-deferred at -r7): DBD::SQLite's Makefile.PL needs an
# already-importable DBI at ITS OWN configure time (it calls into DBI::DBD's
# helper routines) — unblocked by exporting DBI_PUREPERL=2 during the build,
# DBI's own sanctioned pure-perl fallback, so miniperl's `require DBI` under
# Makefile.PL succeeds without dlopen/XSLoader. Build-time only: at boot the
# real compiled-in DBI XS loads via the same static_ext bootstrap table every
# other baked module uses. DBD::SQLite links its OWN bundled sqlite
# amalgamation (3.51.1), not monolith-sqlite's libsqlite3.a, because
# DBD::SQLite's Makefile.PL keeps the system-sqlite path behind a permanent
# `if ( 0 )` upstream. The guestbook still talks to SQLite via the on-disc
# `sqlite3` CLI (dev-db/monolith-sqlite, P1) for its persistence, not DBI —
# see scripts/boot-test.py's smoke_perl_dbi for DBI's own (separate)
# in-memory acceptance check.
dev-lang/monolith-perl

